OL,7,GPart of theBfunAofCtramppolineEchoosing
OL,8, luridFcolours.GTeletext uses invisible 
OL,9, characters to change the colour. This  
OL,10, means that youGneed to leave a space   
OL,11, before the text that you want coloured.
OL,12,C                                       
OL,13,GAove the cursor to the left of the part
OL,14, you want coloured and press escape and 
OL,15, the first letter of the colour name.   
OL,16,Aesc-rBesc-gCesc-yDesc-bEesc-cFesc-m    
OL,17, esc-w               @                  
OL,18,CFor black you use esc-k.GButtG @OL!    
OL,19,Cwhich you  an see bet@er on aG         
OL,20,C]@background any colour but black      
OL,21,FComing soon:Ared,Dblue,Cyellow,Emagenta
OL,22,Gand last but not least,Fcyan@          
OL,24, A Next BIndex    CFlash    FReveal     
